3. The learned Counsel appearing for the appellant has urged two grounds in support of the appeal. Firstly, that the Summary Military Court which passed the original order of conviction and sentence was not a Court within the meaning of Section 386 of the Code of Criminal Procedure and as such the sentence of fine imposed upon the, appellant could not be executed as a, decree. Secondly, he has argued that the order of amnesty issued by the Government covered the sentence of fine as well and as such the appellant was not liable for the fine The learned Deputy Attorney General has, however, argued with reference to the Martial Law regulation No. 2(c) that the Summary Military Courts established under the Martial Law Regulation exercised the same powers and followed the same procedure as a Summary Court Marshal under the Pakistan Army Act, 1952 and the provisions of that Act and the Rules made there under applied to all such proceedings. Section 142 of the Army Act, 1952 relating to execution of sentence of fine laid down as follows:— 

 "(3) Where the Courts issue a warrant to the Collector under sub-section (1) clause (b) such warrant shall be deemed to be a decree, and, the Collector to be the decree-holder, within the meaning of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, and the nearest Civil Court by which any decree for a like amount could be executed shall, for the purpose of the said Code, be deemed to be the Court which passed the decree, and all the provisions of that Code as to execution of decree shall apply accordingly; 

 5. In the instant case, a warrant in respect of the sentence of fine was forwarded to the Collector of the District who as the decree-holder sent it to the Sub-ordinate Judge for execution of the same and accordingly the instant proceeding was started. Having regard to the provisions of Army Act which have been made applicable in the case of Summary Military Courts and the Code of Criminal Procedure, we are of the opinion that there was no illegality in executing the decree passed by the Summary Military Court in respect of the sentence of fine in accordance with the procedure laid down under the Code of Criminal Procedure.
